# Snippet projects that are not canonically formatted yet.
#
# scripts/check-book-format.sh reports these without failing. Everything not
# listed here is gated: a new snippet, or an edit to an already-canonical one,
# must be `bynkc fmt` clean.
#
# These chapters predate the formatter. They cannot be reformatted mechanically:
# chapters 6-10 and 12 print listings by slicing hard-coded line ranges out of
# these files — `source-lines(path, start, end)`, 21 call sites — and formatting
# shifts every line number. Chapter 7's ranges run off the end of the reformatted
# file and fail the Typst build; the rest silently print the wrong lines. So each
# of these needs `bynkc fmt` *and* its chapter's ranges re-derived, with the
# typeset result read. Reformatting also collapses single-expression bodies onto
# one line, which widens some listings past the code column.
#
# This is a ratchet. A project here that has become canonical fails the gate with
# a note to delete its line, so the list can only shrink and cannot go stale.
#
# One project path per line, relative to snippets/.
